  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Reflective in Dativa",
   "texto": [
    "In **Ich wasche mich**, the reflexive pronoun is accusative. If the action includes a part of the body as a direct object, the reflexive goes in dative: **Ich wasche mir die Hände**.",
    "It is not a rule for any complement: the verb and its other objects determine the case. With parts of the body it is usually used: **die Hände**, not «meine Hände»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Shopping and your own things",
   "texto": [
    "**Ich kaufe mir ein Auto** (I buy a car). **Ich putze mir die Zähne** (I brush my teeth). **Du bürstest dir die Haare** (you brush your hair).",
    "As soon as you know the complement, the reflexive changes: mich → mir."
   ]
